---
layout: base.njk
title: Compare
permalink: /compare/
description: Atomdrift Scan vs Socket, Aikido, SafeDep, VirusTotal and ClamAV on live zero-day supply-chain malware. Measured daily on an identical cohort, every sample published.
---

<style>
  .compare { max-width: 1000px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 4px 24px 64px; }

  /* one bar palette for every engine: hostile solid, suspicious pale, grey = unreadable.
     Atomdrift is marked by its label, not by a colour of its own. */
  :root {
    --h: #9abe25; --s: #cfe09a; --na: #dfe3e8; --e: #d64545;
    --t-hostile: #dc2626; --t-suspicious: #e0a526; --t-benign: #2f9e63; --t-nodata: #7b8494;
  }

  /* ---------- hero ---------- */
  /* Keep the proof card compact: at the full page width this makes it about 30%
     narrower than the old 1.45fr/1fr split and gives the badge row one clean line. */
  .cmp-hero { display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) minmax(240px, 28.5%); gap: 28px;
              align-items: start; padding: 18px 0 4px; }
  .cmp-hero .kick { font-family: 'Oxanium', sans-serif; font-size: .7rem; font-weight: 800; letter-spacing: .15em;
                    text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--slate); margin-bottom: 9px; }
  /* No hard break: a <br> splits at the same word whatever the column width, which
     is why it read as arbitrary. balance lets the browser even out the lines itself. */
  .cmp-hero h1 { font-family: 'Oxanium', sans-serif; font-size: 2.15rem; font-weight: 800; color: var(--carbon);
                 letter-spacing: -1.1px; line-height: 1.03; margin: 0; text-wrap: balance; }
  .cmp-hero h1 em { font-style: normal; color: var(--atomdrift-blue); }
  .cmp-hero .say { margin: 12px 0 0; color: var(--iron); line-height: 1.6; font-size: .95rem; }
  .cmp-hero .say b { color: var(--carbon); font-weight: 600; }
  .cta-row { display: flex; gap: 9px; flex-wrap: wrap; margin: 15px 0 0; }
  .cta { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; font-family: 'Oxanium', sans-serif; font-weight: 700;
         font-size: .82rem; padding: 8px 15px; border-radius: 7px; text-decoration: none;
         min-height: 44px; border: 1.5px solid var(--border); color: var(--carbon);
         transition: border-color .15s, color .15s, background .15s; }
  .cta:hover { border-color: var(--atomdrift-blue); color: var(--atomdrift-blue); }
  .cta-primary { background: var(--toxic); border-color: var(--toxic); color: var(--carbon); font-weight: 800; }
  .cta-primary:hover { background: var(--toxic-dark); border-color: var(--toxic-dark); color: #fff; }
  .instl { margin-top: 11px; font-family: 'SF Mono', Consolas, monospace; font-size: .78rem; background: var(--mist);
           border-radius: 6px; padding: 8px 12px; color: var(--carbon); overflow-x: auto; }
  .badges { display: flex; gap: 6px; flex-wrap: wrap; margin-top: 12px; }
  .bdg { font-family: 'Oxanium', sans-serif; font-size: .68rem; font-weight: 800; letter-spacing: .05em;
         text-transform: uppercase; border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 5px; padding: 3px 8px;
         color: var(--iron); white-space: nowrap; }  /* or 'illumos' orphans onto its own line */
  .bdg.hot { border-color: var(--toxic-dark); color: var(--toxic-dark); background: var(--toxic-dim); }

  /* Our own two numbers, not a face-off. The comparison lives in the leaderboard
     directly below; repeating it here cost width the headline column needed. */
  .proof { background: var(--carbon); border-radius: 12px; padding: 18px 20px; color: #fff;
           display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 12px; }
  .proof .scores { display: flex; gap: 26px; }
  .proof .n { font-family: 'Oxanium', sans-serif; font-size: 2.7rem; font-weight: 800; line-height: .85;
              letter-spacing: -2px; color: var(--toxic); font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }
  .proof .n.fp { color: #fff; }
  .proof .l { font-size: .68rem; font-weight: 800; letter-spacing: .09em; color: #b9bfc9; margin-top: 8px;
              text-transform: uppercase; font-family: 'Oxanium', sans-serif; }
  .proof .at { font-family: 'SF Mono', Consolas, monospace; font-size: .72rem; color: #d5d9d2;
               border-top: 1px solid #2a2e28; padding-top: 11px; }
  .proof .at b { color: var(--toxic); font-weight: 700; }
  .proof .dial { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 7px; }
  .proof .dial-label { color: #d5d9d2; font-family: 'Oxanium', sans-serif; font-size: .7rem;
                       font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: .04em; }
  .proof input[type=range] { -webkit-appearance: none; appearance: none; width: 100%; background: transparent;
                             height: 44px; margin: 0; cursor: ew-resize; }
  .proof input[type=range]::-webkit-slider-runnable-track { height: 3px; border-radius: 2px; background: #71787f; }
  .proof input[type=range]::-moz-range-track { height: 3px; border-radius: 2px; background: #71787f; }
  .proof input[type=range]::-webkit-slider-thumb { -webkit-appearance: none; width: 20px; height: 20px;
    border-radius: 50%; background: var(--toxic); margin-top: -8.5px; transition: transform .12s ease; }
  .proof input[type=range]::-moz-range-thumb { width: 20px; height: 20px; border: 0; border-radius: 50%;
    background: var(--toxic); transition: transform .12s ease; }
  .proof input[type=range]:hover::-webkit-slider-thumb { transform: scale(1.25); }
  .proof input[type=range]:hover::-moz-range-thumb { transform: scale(1.25); }
  .proof input[type=range]:focus-visible { outline: 2px solid var(--toxic); outline-offset: 5px; border-radius: 4px; }
  .proof .ends { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; font-family: 'SF Mono', Consolas, monospace;
                 font-size: .68rem; color: #b9bfc9; }
  .proof p { margin: 0; font-size: .74rem; line-height: 1.55; color: #b9bfc9; }
  .proof p b { color: #eef0f3; font-weight: 600; }

  /* ---------- sections ---------- */
  .compare h2 { font-family: 'Oxanium', sans-serif; font-size: 1.05rem; font-weight: 800; color: var(--carbon);
                border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border); padding-bottom: 6px; margin: 40px 0 4px; letter-spacing: -.3px;
                display: flex; align-items: baseline; gap: 9px; flex-wrap: wrap; }
  .compare h2 .note { font-family: 'Inter', sans-serif; font-size: .72rem; font-weight: 400; color: var(--slate); }
  /* Page-level copy should use the content width. The hero's grid already gives
     its copy a readable measure; another max-width here only creates a ragged,
     half-empty column below full-width charts. */
  .compare .sub { color: var(--iron); font-size: .88rem; margin: 10px 0 14px; }
  .compare .sub b { color: var(--carbon); font-weight: 600; }

  /* ---------- bars ---------- */
  .rows { display: grid; grid-template-columns: max-content 1fr max-content; gap: 6px 12px; align-items: center; margin: 12px 0 8px; }
  .rows .rn { font-family: 'Oxanium', sans-serif; font-weight: 600; font-size: .8rem; white-space: nowrap; color: var(--graphite); }
  .rows .rn.us { color: var(--atomdrift-blue); font-weight: 800; }
  .rows .tr { height: 17px; background: var(--mist); border-radius: 4px; overflow: hidden; display: flex;
              box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 1px rgba(0,0,0,.05); }
  .rows .hb, .legend .hostile-key { background: var(--h); }
  .rows .hb, .rows .sb, .rows .un { height: 100%; }
  .rows .sb, .legend .suspicious-key { background-color: var(--s);
    background-image: repeating-linear-gradient(135deg, rgba(0,0,0,.18) 0 2px, transparent 2px 5px); }
  .rows .un, .legend .unsupported-key { background-color: var(--na);
    background-image: repeating-linear-gradient(90deg, rgba(0,0,0,.2) 0 1px, transparent 1px 4px); }
  .rows .eb, .legend .errored-key { background: var(--e); }
  /* One failure in a hundred is a sub-pixel sliver of bar, which is a tooltip
     nobody can land on; 5px keeps it aimable without reading as a real share. */
  .rows .eb { height: 100%; min-width: 5px; cursor: help; }
  /* Grey (scope) and red (failure) anchor right, in that order; whichever comes
     first takes the auto margin so the pair hugs the right edge either way. */
  .rows .un, .rows .sb + .eb, .rows .hb + .eb, .rows .eb:first-child { margin-left: auto; }
  .rows .un + .eb { margin-left: 0; }
  .rows .rv { font-family: 'Oxanium', sans-serif; font-weight: 800; font-size: .8rem; font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
              text-align: right; min-width: 36px; color: var(--carbon); }
  .legend { display: flex; gap: 8px 16px; flex-wrap: wrap; align-items: center; font-size: .72rem; color: var(--iron); }
  .legend i { width: 11px; height: 11px; border-radius: 2px; display: inline-block; margin-right: 5px; vertical-align: -1px; }
  .fig-note { color: var(--slate); font-size: .74rem; line-height: 1.55; margin: 8px 0 0; }
  .fig-note b { color: var(--graphite); }
  .fig-note a { color: var(--slate); }
  .lnk { color: var(--atomdrift-blue); text-decoration: underline; text-underline-offset: 2px; white-space: nowrap; }

  /* ---------- frontier ---------- */
  .frontier-wrap { margin: 14px 0 4px; overflow-x: auto; }
  .frontier-wrap svg { width: 100%; min-width: 720px; height: auto; display: block; }
  .q-grid { stroke: var(--border); stroke-width: 1; }
  /* Solid hairlines throughout: a dashed rule reads as "projection" or "threshold"
     when it is only ever a grid or a divider. */
  .q-axis, .q-div { stroke: #c9ccd1; stroke-width: 1; }
  .q-tick { fill: var(--slate); font-size: 10.5px; font-family: system-ui, sans-serif; }
  .q-head { fill: var(--carbon); font-size: 20px; font-weight: 800; font-family: 'Oxanium', sans-serif;
            letter-spacing: -.4px; }
  .q-headsub { fill: var(--iron); font-size: 13px; font-family: 'Inter', system-ui, sans-serif; }
  .q-alab { fill: var(--carbon); font-size: 13px; font-weight: 700; font-family: 'Oxanium', sans-serif; }
  .q-asub { fill: var(--slate); font-size: 10.5px; font-family: system-ui, sans-serif; }
  .q-target { fill: #2a78d6; opacity: .07; }
  .q-target-edge { fill: none; stroke: #bcd8f2; stroke-width: 1; }
  .q-quad { fill: #1e6bb8; font-size: 10px; font-weight: 800; letter-spacing: .08em;
            font-family: 'Oxanium', sans-serif; }
  .q-leader { stroke: #c9ccd1; stroke-width: 1; }
  .q-pt { stroke: #fff; stroke-width: 2; }
  /* Every rival is drawn the same: Atomdrift is the only emphasized mark, and the
     emphasis is size and weight, never hue — an engine keeps the colour it has in
     the bars and the trend chart. */
  .q-name { fill: var(--slate); font-size: 11px; font-weight: 500; font-family: 'Oxanium', sans-serif; }
  .q-usname { fill: var(--carbon); font-size: 13px; font-weight: 800; font-family: 'Oxanium', sans-serif; }
  /* The cost line under a label, in one desaturated status red wherever it appears. */
  .q-fp { fill: #b0473b; font-size: 9.5px; font-weight: 600; font-family: 'Oxanium', sans-serif; }
  /* Solid, because it is a measured frontier rather than "anywhere along here";
     the gradient tail marks where the budget starts costing something. */
  .q-curve { fill: none; stroke: url(#q-curve-grad); stroke-width: 3;
             stroke-linecap: round; stroke-linejoin: round; }
  /* Outline rings so a coincident rival dot stays visible inside them. */
  .q-cpt { fill: #fff; stroke-width: 2.5; }
  /* The axis break: a surface-coloured stroke under a hairline, so the two slashes
     read as a cut in the axis rather than as marks floating beside it. */
  .q-break-mask { stroke: #fff; stroke-width: 5; }
  .q-break { stroke: #c9ccd1; stroke-width: 1; }

  /* ---------- the difference matrix ---------- */
  /* Three rows, two columns: the least text that still makes a comparison. Each
     cell is one sentence, so the whole argument is scannable in a column sweep. */
  .diffs { display: grid; grid-template-columns: max-content 1fr 1fr; gap: 1px; margin-top: 10px;
           background: var(--border); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 10px; overflow: hidden; }
  .diffs > * { background: #fff; padding: 11px 15px; }
  .diffs .dh { font-family: 'Oxanium', sans-serif; font-size: .68rem; font-weight: 800; letter-spacing: .09em;
               text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--slate); padding-top: 12px; padding-bottom: 10px; }
  .diffs .dh.us { color: var(--toxic-dark); background: var(--toxic-dim); }
  .diffs .dk { font-family: 'Oxanium', sans-serif; font-size: .82rem; font-weight: 800; color: var(--carbon);
               white-space: nowrap; }
  .diffs .dv { font-size: .8rem; line-height: 1.5; color: var(--slate); }
  .diffs .dv.us { color: var(--carbon); background: var(--toxic-dim); }
  .diffs .dv b { color: var(--carbon); font-weight: 650; }

  /* ---------- coverage table ---------- */
  .tw { overflow-x: auto; margin-top: 12px; }
  table.cov { border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; min-width: 520px; font-size: .8rem; }
  table.cov th, table.cov td { text-align: right; padding: 7px 12px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
                               font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }
  table.cov thead th { font-family: 'Oxanium', sans-serif; font-size: .66rem; letter-spacing: .07em;
                       text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--slate); font-weight: 700; }
  table.cov tbody th { text-align: left; font-weight: 600; color: var(--graphite); white-space: nowrap; }
  table.cov tbody th i { display: inline-block; width: 8px; height: 8px; border-radius: 50%; margin-right: 8px; }
  table.cov .muted { color: var(--slate); }

  /* ---------- trend ---------- */
  .trend-wrap { position: relative; height: 340px; margin-top: 10px; }

  /* ---------- samples + method ---------- */
  /* Folded by default: it is the evidence, not the argument. Anyone who wants to
     check the work opens it; nobody else has to scroll past 43 filenames. */
  details.appendix { margin-top: 40px; border-top: 1px solid var(--border); padding-top: 6px; }
  details.appendix > summary { cursor: pointer; list-style: none; display: flex; align-items: baseline; gap: 9px;
    flex-wrap: wrap; font-family: 'Oxanium', sans-serif; font-weight: 800; font-size: 1.05rem; color: var(--carbon);
    min-height: 44px; padding: 8px 0; letter-spacing: -.3px; }
  details.appendix > summary::-webkit-details-marker { display: none; }
  details.appendix > summary::before { content: "▸"; color: var(--toxic-dark); font-size: .8rem; transition: transform .15s ease; }
  details.appendix[open] > summary::before { transform: rotate(90deg); }
  details.appendix > summary:hover { color: var(--atomdrift-blue); }
  details.appendix > summary:focus-visible { outline: 3px solid var(--atomdrift-blue); outline-offset: 3px; border-radius: 3px; }
  .samples { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 2px 22px; font-family: 'SF Mono', Consolas, monospace;
             font-size: .74rem; margin-top: 10px; }
  .samples a { color: var(--atomdrift-blue); text-decoration: none; white-space: nowrap; overflow: hidden;
               text-overflow: ellipsis; display: flex; align-items: center; min-height: 28px; }
  .samples a::before { content: "▪ "; color: var(--h); }
  .samples a:hover { text-decoration: underline; }
  .meth { background: var(--cream); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 8px; padding: 12px 15px;
          font-size: .78rem; color: var(--graphite); line-height: 1.65; margin-top: 14px; }
  .meth b { color: var(--carbon); font-family: 'Oxanium', sans-serif; }
  .closer { margin-top: 34px; background: var(--carbon); border-radius: 12px; padding: 20px 24px; display: flex;
            justify-content: space-between; align-items: center; gap: 20px; flex-wrap: wrap; }
  .closer h3 { color: #fff; font-size: 1.05rem; letter-spacing: -.5px; margin: 0; font-family: 'Oxanium', sans-serif; font-weight: 800; }
  .closer p { margin: 5px 0 0; color: #b9bfc9; font-size: .78rem; }
  .closer .inst { font-family: 'SF Mono', Consolas, monospace; font-size: .78rem; background: #1c1f1a; color: var(--toxic);
                  border-radius: 7px; padding: 10px 15px; }

  @media (max-width: 720px) {
    .cmp-hero { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 20px; }
    .samples { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .diffs { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .diffs .dh:first-child { display: none; }
    .cmp-hero h1 { font-size: 1.7rem; }
    .samples a { min-height: 44px; }
  }
</style>

{# One palette for every engine — hostile solid, suspicious pale, both anchored left;
   a grey tail on the right for unsupported file formats, which the methodology
   scores as a miss. Atomdrift is identified by its label, not by a colour of its own. #}
{%- macro rows(board, cohort) -%}
  <div class="rows">
  {%- for s in board | byFlagged %}
    {%- set p = providers[s.scanner] %}
    {%- set unsup = s.unsupported or 0 %}
    <div class="rn{% if s.scanner == 'ascan' %} us{% endif %}">{{ p.name or s.scanner }}</div>
    <div class="tr" role="img" aria-label="{{ p.name or s.scanner }}: {{ s.hostile }} hostile, {{ s.suspicious }} suspicious, {{ s.benign }} analyzed clean{% if s.nodata %}, {{ s.nodata }} no record{% endif %}{% if s.errored %}, {{ s.errored }} errored{% endif %}{% if unsup %}, {{ unsup }} unsupported file format{% endif %}" title="{{ s.hostile }} hostile · {{ s.suspicious }} suspicious · {{ s.benign }} analyzed clean{% if s.nodata %} · {{ s.nodata }} no record{% endif %}{% if s.errored %} · {{ s.errored }} errored{% endif %}{% if unsup %} · {{ unsup }} unsupported file format{% endif %}">
      {%- if s.supported > 0 -%}
        {%- if s.hostile > 0 %}<span class="hb" style="width:{{ s.hostile / s.supported * 100 }}%"></span>{% endif -%}
        {%- if s.suspicious > 0 %}<span class="sb" style="width:{{ s.suspicious / s.supported * 100 }}%"></span>{% endif -%}
        {%- if unsup > 0 %}<span class="un" style="width:{{ unsup / s.supported * 100 }}%"></span>{% endif -%}
        {#- The red segment names its own casualties: which samples the engine
            failed to read, and what it said. Its own title beats the row's. -#}
        {%- if s.errored > 0 %}{% set errs = battle.samples | errorLines(s.scanner, cohort) %}<span class="eb" style="width:{{ s.errored / s.supported * 100 }}%" role="img" aria-label="{{ p.name or s.scanner }} errored on {{ s.errored }} sample{{ 's' if s.errored != 1 }}: {{ errs | join('; ') }}" title="errored on {{ s.errored }} sample{{ 's' if s.errored != 1 }}
{%- for l in errs %}
{{ l }}
{%- endfor %}"></span>{% endif -%}
      {%- endif -%}
    </div>
    {%- if s.supported %}
    <div class="rv">{{ (100 * (s.hostile + s.suspicious) / s.supported) | round(0) }}%</div>
    {%- else %}
    <div class="rv" style="color:var(--slate)">—</div>
    {%- endif %}
  {%- endfor %}
  </div>
{%- endmacro -%}

<div class="main-full compare">

  {%- set h = battle | headline %}
  {%- set curve = battle | ascanCurve %}

  <div class="cmp-hero">
    <div>
      <div class="kick">Atomdrift Scan · zero-day supply-chain malware detection · Apache-2.0</div>
      <h1>Supply-chain malware detection for <em>your</em> code, not just a vendor's index.</h1>
      <p class="say">Every hosted scanner answers one question: <b>is this package on our list yet?</b> Atomdrift reads
        the artifact — source, binaries, containers, archives, private packages — and scores what it can actually do.
        Nothing to be listed on, nothing to wait for, and it works on the code no vendor indexes.</p>
      <div class="cta-row">
        <a class="cta cta-primary" href="https://install.atomdrift.org/">Install it →</a>
        <a class="cta" href="#how">The differences</a>
        <a class="cta" href="#samples">Every sample</a>
      </div>
      <div class="instl">curl -fsSL https://install.atomdrift.org/scan.sh | sh</div>
      <div class="badges">
        <span class="bdg hot">Apache-2.0</span>
        <span class="bdg">100+ file types</span>
        <span class="bdg">{{ providers.ascan.registries | length }} registries</span>
        <span class="bdg">no telemetry</span>
        {# Longest badge last: it is ~3x the width of the others, so anything after it
           gets stranded alone on the next row. #}
        <span class="bdg">Linux · macOS · BSD · illumos</span>
      </div>
    </div>

    {%- if h %}
    <div class="proof">
      <div class="scores">
        {# "0-day" is the whole claim: signatures and reputation have had no time to
           form on a package published this morning, which is exactly the window a
           supply-chain attack lives in. The cohort line below defines it. #}
        <div><div class="n">{{ h.detRate }}%</div><div class="l">0-day malware caught</div></div>
        {%- if h.fpRate != null %}
        <div><div class="n fp">{{ h.fpRate }}%</div><div class="l">false positives</div></div>
        {%- endif %}
      </div>
      {%- if curve %}
      {%- set dialStop = curve | curveStop(dialDefault) %}
      {# Server-rendered at the shipped default, so the numbers above are right with
         JS off; the slider only ever re-reads values already in the page. #}
      <div class="dial">
        <label class="dial-label" for="dial">False-positive budget</label>
        <input type="range" id="dial" min="0" max="{{ (curve | length) - 1 }}"
               value="{{ curve | curveIndex(dialDefault) }}" step="1"
               aria-valuetext="-l {{ dialStop.l }}: {{ dialStop.det }}% caught, {{ dialStop.flagged }} false positive{% if dialStop.flagged != 1 %}s{% endif %}"
               aria-describedby="dial-help">
        <div class="ends"><span>-l 0</span><span>-l {{ dialMaxLabel }}</span></div>
      </div>
      {%- endif %}
      <div class="at" id="dial-help">at <b id="dial-l">-l {{ dialDefault }}</b> <span id="dial-say">— the shipped default, untuned</span></div>
      <span id="dial-status" class="visually-hidden" aria-live="polite" aria-atomic="true"></span>
      <p><b>{{ battle.generated_at | dateDisplay }}</b> · {{ battle.detection.sample_count }} live samples,
        median <b>{{ battle.malware_age.median_hours | round(0) if battle.malware_age else 24 }} h old</b>.</p>
    </div>
    {%- endif %}
  </div>

  <h2 id="results">Caught, per engine <span class="note">identical cohort · a skip counts as a miss</span></h2>
  {{ rows(battle.detection.leaderboard, 'bad') }}
  <div class="legend">
    <span><i class="hostile-key"></i>flagged hostile</span>
    <span><i class="suspicious-key"></i>flagged suspicious</span>
    <span><i class="unsupported-key"></i>unsupported file format</span>
    <span><i class="errored-key"></i>errored</span>
  </div>
  <p class="fig-note">Every engine is scored at its most sensitive setting, ours included. <b>Grey is scope</b> —
    an engine that only reads registry packages marks the rest of the cohort unsupported, which the methodology
    scores as a miss. <b>Red is failure</b> — the engine supports the sample but errored on it (a timeout or
    crash), which also scores as a miss.</p>

  {%- set q = battle | quadrant(chartProviders) %}
  {%- if q %}
  <h2 id="frontier">Detection vs. false positives <span class="note">every rival ships one setting — <code>-l</code> is a dial you set</span></h2>
  <div class="frontier-wrap">
    <svg viewBox="0 0 {{ q.w }} {{ q.h }}" role="img" aria-label="Zero-day detection rate against false-positive rate for every engine measured this run. The horizontal axis is the share of zero-day malware caught, higher to the right; the vertical axis is false positives, inverted so fewer is higher, and cropped so any engine past the crop appears in a marked strip below. Atomdrift is drawn as a curve across its false-positive budget rather than a single point. Every value follows the chart in a list.">
      {%- if q.curve %}
      <defs>
        <linearGradient id="q-curve-grad" gradientUnits="userSpaceOnUse" x1="{{ q.curve.x1 }}" y1="0" x2="{{ q.curve.x2 }}" y2="0">
          <stop offset="0" stop-color="{{ q.curve.color }}"></stop>
          <stop offset=".6" stop-color="{{ q.curve.color }}"></stop>
          <stop offset="1" stop-color="#c02d1e"></stop>
        </linearGradient>
      </defs>
      {%- endif %}

      {%- if q.head %}
      <text class="q-head" x="{{ q.pl }}" y="{{ q.pt - 66 }}">{{ q.head.title }}</text>
      <text class="q-headsub" x="{{ q.pl }}" y="{{ q.pt - 42 }}">{{ q.head.sub }}</text>
      {%- endif %}

      {# The one shaded region on the chart: high detection, few false positives. #}
      <rect class="q-target" x="{{ q.xDiv }}" y="{{ q.pt }}" width="{{ q.pr - q.xDiv }}" height="{{ q.yDiv - q.pt }}"></rect>
      <rect class="q-target-edge" x="{{ q.xDiv }}" y="{{ q.pt }}" width="{{ q.pr - q.xDiv }}" height="{{ q.yDiv - q.pt }}"></rect>

      {%- for t in q.xTicks %}
      <line class="q-grid" x1="{{ t.x }}" y1="{{ q.pt }}" x2="{{ t.x }}" y2="{{ q.pb }}"></line>
      <text class="q-tick" x="{{ t.x }}" y="{{ q.pb + 20 }}" text-anchor="middle">{{ t.v }}%</text>
      {%- endfor %}
      {%- for t in q.yTicks %}
      <line class="q-grid" x1="{{ q.pl }}" y1="{{ t.y }}" x2="{{ q.pr }}" y2="{{ t.y }}"></line>
      <text class="q-tick" x="{{ q.pl - 9 }}" y="{{ t.y + 4 }}" text-anchor="end">{{ t.v }}%</text>
      {%- endfor %}
      <line class="q-div" x1="{{ q.xDiv }}" y1="{{ q.pt }}" x2="{{ q.xDiv }}" y2="{{ q.mb }}"></line>
      <line class="q-div" x1="{{ q.pl }}" y1="{{ q.yDiv }}" x2="{{ q.pr }}" y2="{{ q.yDiv }}"></line>
      <text class="q-quad" x="{{ q.pr - 10 }}" y="{{ q.yDiv - 10 }}" text-anchor="end">HIGH DETECTION  ·  LOW FALSE POSITIVES</text>

      <line class="q-axis" x1="{{ q.pl }}" y1="{{ q.pt }}" x2="{{ q.pl }}" y2="{{ q.pb }}"></line>
      <line class="q-axis" x1="{{ q.pl }}" y1="{{ q.pb }}" x2="{{ q.pr }}" y2="{{ q.pb }}"></line>
      {# Axis titles carry their own denominator, so no number on the plot needs a
         footnote to be understood. #}
      <text class="q-alab" x="{{ (q.pl + q.pr) / 2 }}" y="{{ q.pb + 46 }}" text-anchor="middle">Zero-day malware caught  ·  more is better →</text>
      <text class="q-asub" x="{{ (q.pl + q.pr) / 2 }}" y="{{ q.pb + 62 }}" text-anchor="middle">of {{ q.nBad }} malicious packages, none more than 48 hours old</text>
      <g transform="translate(24,{{ (q.pt + q.pb) / 2 }}) rotate(-90)">
        <text class="q-alab" x="0" y="0" text-anchor="middle">False positives  ·  fewer is better ↑</text>
        <text class="q-asub" x="0" y="15" text-anchor="middle">of {{ q.nGood }} known-safe packages</text>
      </g>

      {%- if q.curve %}
      <path class="q-curve" d="{{ q.curve.path }}"></path>
      {%- endif %}

      {%- for m in q.marks %}
      {%- if m.leader %}<line class="q-leader" x1="{{ m.leader.x1 }}" y1="{{ m.leader.y1 }}" x2="{{ m.leader.x2 }}" y2="{{ m.leader.y2 }}"></line>{% endif %}
      {%- endfor %}

      {# Rivals are drawn identically to one another — Atomdrift is the only
         emphasized mark, and emphasis is size and weight, never hue. #}
      {%- for m in q.marks %}
      {%- if m.kind == 'engine' %}
      <circle class="q-pt" cx="{{ m.x }}" cy="{{ m.y }}" r="{{ m.r }}" fill="{{ m.engine.color }}">
        <title>{{ m.engine.name }} — {{ m.engine.det }}% caught ({{ m.engine.caught }}/{{ m.engine.nBad }}), {{ m.engine.flagged }} false positive{% if m.engine.flagged != 1 %}s{% endif %} of {{ m.engine.nGood }}</title>
      </circle>
      {%- else %}
      <circle class="q-cpt" cx="{{ m.x }}" cy="{{ m.y }}" r="{{ m.r }}" stroke="{{ q.curve.color }}">
        <title>atomscan -l {{ m.stop.lLo }}{% if m.stop.lHi != m.stop.lLo %}–{{ m.stop.lHi }}{% endif %} — {{ m.stop.det }}% caught ({{ m.stop.caught }}/{{ q.nBad }}), {{ m.stop.flagged }} false positive{% if m.stop.flagged != 1 %}s{% endif %} of {{ q.nGood }}</title>
      </circle>
      {%- endif %}
      {%- endfor %}

      {%- for m in q.marks %}
      <text class="{{ 'q-usname' if m.kind == 'stop' else 'q-name' }}" x="{{ m.label.tx }}" y="{{ m.label.y1 }}" text-anchor="{{ m.label.anchor }}">{{ m.head }}</text>
      {%- if m.sub %}<text class="q-fp" x="{{ m.label.tx }}" y="{{ m.label.y2 }}" text-anchor="{{ m.label.anchor }}">{{ m.sub }}</text>{% endif %}
      {%- endfor %}

      {# Anything past the crop keeps its real value in a labelled strip below an
         axis break, rather than being clipped to the frame and understated. #}
      {%- if q.offscale | length %}
      <line class="q-grid" x1="{{ q.pl }}" y1="{{ q.breakY }}" x2="{{ q.pr }}" y2="{{ q.breakY }}"></line>
      <line class="q-break-mask" x1="{{ q.pl - 6 }}" y1="{{ q.breakY + 8 }}" x2="{{ q.pl + 5 }}" y2="{{ q.breakY - 8 }}"></line>
      <line class="q-break" x1="{{ q.pl - 6 }}" y1="{{ q.breakY + 8 }}" x2="{{ q.pl + 5 }}" y2="{{ q.breakY - 8 }}"></line>
      <line class="q-break-mask" x1="{{ q.pl + 2 }}" y1="{{ q.breakY + 8 }}" x2="{{ q.pl + 13 }}" y2="{{ q.breakY - 8 }}"></line>
      <line class="q-break" x1="{{ q.pl + 2 }}" y1="{{ q.breakY + 8 }}" x2="{{ q.pl + 13 }}" y2="{{ q.breakY - 8 }}"></line>
      {%- for o in q.offscale %}
      <text class="q-tick" x="{{ q.pl - 9 }}" y="{{ o.y + 4 }}" text-anchor="end">{{ o.engine.fp }}%</text>
      <circle class="q-pt" cx="{{ o.x }}" cy="{{ o.y }}" r="5" fill="{{ o.engine.color }}">
        <title>{{ o.engine.name }} — {{ o.engine.det }}% caught, {{ o.engine.flagged }} false positive{% if o.engine.flagged != 1 %}s{% endif %} of {{ o.engine.nGood }}</title>
      </circle>
      <text class="q-name" x="{{ o.x + 13 }}" y="{{ o.y - 2 }}">{{ o.engine.name }}  {{ o.engine.det }}%</text>
      {%- if o.fpText %}<text class="q-fp" x="{{ o.x + 13 }}" y="{{ o.y + 12 }}">{{ o.fpText }}</text>{% endif %}
      {%- endfor %}
      {%- endif %}
    </svg>
  </div>
  <div class="visually-hidden">
    <h3>Detection and false-positive chart data</h3>
    <ul>
      {%- for m in q.marks %}
        {%- if m.kind == 'engine' %}<li>{{ m.engine.name }}: {{ m.engine.det }}% caught ({{ m.engine.caught }} of {{ m.engine.nBad }}), {{ m.engine.flagged }} false positive{% if m.engine.flagged != 1 %}s{% endif %} of {{ m.engine.nGood }}.</li>{% endif %}
      {%- endfor %}
      {%- for o in q.offscale %}<li>{{ o.engine.name }}: {{ o.engine.det }}% caught, {{ o.engine.flagged }} false positive{% if o.engine.flagged != 1 %}s{% endif %} of {{ o.engine.nGood }}.</li>{% endfor %}
      {%- if q.curve %}
        {%- for v in q.curve.verts %}<li>Atomdrift at -l {{ v.lLo }}{% if v.lHi != v.lLo %} through {{ v.lHi }}{% endif %}: {{ v.det }}% caught ({{ v.caught }} of {{ q.nBad }}), {{ v.flagged }} false positive{% if v.flagged != 1 %}s{% endif %} of {{ q.nGood }}.</li>{% endfor %}
      {%- endif %}
    </ul>
  </div>
  {%- if q.curve %}
  <p class="fig-note"><code>-l</code> is a false-positive budget — files flagged per <b>100 million</b>, calibrated per
    file type. Not “medium sensitivity”; a number you can plan a pipeline around. The curve runs
    <code>-l 0</code> to <code>-l {{ dialMaxLabel }}</code> through
    <b>{{ q.curve.verts | length }} measured operating points</b>, spans between them interpolated.</p>
  {%- endif %}
  <p class="fig-note">False-positive axis inverted and cropped at {{ q.yMax }}%
    {%- if q.offscale | length %}; {% for o in q.offscale %}{{ o.engine.name }}{% if not loop.last %}, {% endif %}{% endfor %}
    {{ 'is' if (q.offscale | length) == 1 else 'are' }} past it, drawn below the break at
    {% for o in q.offscale %}{{ o.engine.fp }}%{% if not loop.last %} and {% endif %}{% endfor %}{% endif %}.
    Hover any mark for exact counts.</p>
  {%- endif %}

  <h2 id="over-time">Every previous run <span class="note">a fresh cohort each time</span></h2>
  <p class="sub">Most engines swing sixty points as the samples change. <b>Judge us on the worst night, not the
    best.</b></p>
  {%- if history and history | length >= 2 %}
  <div class="trend-wrap"><canvas id="trendChart" role="img" aria-label="Historical 0-day catch-rate line chart for every measured engine across fresh live-malware cohorts. Current-run values are provided in Latest results above."></canvas></div>
  <script src="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/chart.js@4.4.1/dist/chart.umd.min.js"></script>
  <script>
  (function () {
    // Truncate to the 2026-07-09 10:00 UTC pipeline overhaul: earlier runs measured a
    // materially different detection stack, so plotting them would misrepresent the
    // current engines. Non-destructive — history.json keeps every point.
    const CUTOFF = Date.parse('2026-07-09T10:00:00Z');
    const H = ({{ history | dump | safe }}).filter(p => Date.parse(p.at) >= CUTOFF);
    const PROV = {{ chartProviders | dump | safe }};
    // Engine colors and draw order come from providers.json — one declaration
    // shared with the quadrant, so an engine keeps its hue across the page and
    // no engine can be missing from this chart just by being absent from a map
    // hardcoded here.
    const ENGINES = Object.keys(PROV).filter(e => !PROV[e].hidden)
      .sort((a, b) => (PROV[a].slot || 99) - (PROV[b].slot || 99));
    const COLOR = Object.fromEntries(ENGINES.map(e => [e, PROV[e].color || '#6b7280']));
    const US = 'ascan';
    const labels = H.map(p => new Date(p.at).toLocaleString(undefined, { month: 'short', day: 'numeric', hour: 'numeric' }));
    // Atomdrift is the subject: drawn last (on top) and heavier than the field.
    // The emphasis is weight only — fading the others toward the surface used to
    // collapse them into each other (seven lines at 45% alpha sit ~7 ΔE apart,
    // under the ~15 a full-color reader needs), so every line keeps its own hue.
    const order = ENGINES.filter(e => e !== US).concat(US);
    const datasets = order.map(e => {
      const us = e === US;
      return {
        label: (PROV[e] && (PROV[e].chartName || PROV[e].name)) || e,
        data: H.map(p => (p.detection && p.detection[e] != null) ? Math.round(p.detection[e] * 100) : null),
        solidColor: COLOR[e],
        borderColor: COLOR[e],
        backgroundColor: COLOR[e],
        borderWidth: us ? 4 : 2,
        pointRadius: us ? 4 : 2.5,
        pointHoverRadius: us ? 6 : 4,
        tension: 0.25, spanGaps: true
      };
    }).filter(d => d.data.some(v => v != null));

    // Each line's latest value, labelled at its right end so current standings read
    // without hovering; labels are nudged apart vertically when they'd collide.
    const endLabels = {
      id: 'endLabels',
      afterDatasetsDraw(chart) {
        const ctx = chart.ctx;
        const items = [];
        chart.data.datasets.forEach((ds, i) => {
          const meta = chart.getDatasetMeta(i);
          if (meta.hidden || !meta.data.length) return;
          for (let j = ds.data.length - 1; j >= 0; j--) {
            if (ds.data[j] != null) {
              items.push({ x: meta.data[j].x, y: meta.data[j].y, val: ds.data[j], color: ds.solidColor, bold: ds.borderWidth >= 3 });
              break;
            }
          }
        });
        items.sort((a, b) => a.y - b.y);
        for (let i = 1; i < items.length; i++) {
          if (items[i].y - items[i - 1].y < 13) items[i].y = items[i - 1].y + 13;
        }
        ctx.save();
        ctx.textBaseline = 'middle';
        items.forEach(it => {
          ctx.font = (it.bold ? '700 ' : '600 ') + '11px system-ui, sans-serif';
          ctx.fillStyle = '#404040';
          ctx.fillText(it.val + '%', it.x + 7, it.y);
        });
        ctx.restore();
      }
    };

    new Chart(document.getElementById('trendChart'), {
      type: 'line',
      data: { labels, datasets },
      plugins: [endLabels],
      options: {
        responsive: true, maintainAspectRatio: false,
        interaction: { mode: 'index', intersect: false },
        layout: { padding: { right: 46, left: 6 } },
        scales: {
          y: { beginAtZero: true, max: 100, ticks: { callback: v => v + '%' }, title: { display: true, text: '0-day catch rate' } }
        },
        plugins: {
          // Chart.js defaults to a 40px line-style box per entry, which pushes
          // eight engines onto three rows and eats the chart's height. Small
          // circular swatches keep the whole field on one or two rows.
          legend: {
            position: 'bottom',
            labels: {
              usePointStyle: true, pointStyle: 'circle', boxWidth: 8, boxHeight: 8, padding: 12, font: { size: 11 },
              // VirusTotal's engine count earns its width on a full-size chart, but
              // the eight entries only just fit one row — adding "[66 engines]" tips
              // them onto a second row once the canvas drops below ~730px, which
              // comes straight out of the plot's height. Under that, fall back to the
              // bare name: the count is still on the quadrant and the bars. Chart.js
              // regenerates labels on resize, so this re-evaluates as the page reflows.
              generateLabels(chart) {
                const items = Chart.defaults.plugins.legend.labels.generateLabels(chart);
                if (chart.width < 730) {
                  for (const it of items) it.text = it.text.replace(/ \[\d+ engines\]$/, '');
                }
                return items;
              }
            }
          },
          tooltip: {
            itemSort: (a, b) => b.parsed.y - a.parsed.y,
            callbacks: { label: c => `${c.dataset.label}: ${c.parsed.y}%` }
          }
        }
      }
    });
  })();
  </script>
  {%- else %}
  <div class="meth">Historical trend is collecting. Each recorded run appends a snapshot; the chart appears once there
    are at least two.</div>
  {%- endif %}

  <h2 id="how">Three structural differences <span class="note">architecture, not features</span></h2>
  <div class="diffs">
    <div class="dh"></div>
    <div class="dh">Hosted scanners</div>
    <div class="dh us">Atomdrift</div>

    <div class="dk">Scope</div>
    <div class="dv">Public packages, or file hashes, that they already index.</div>
    <div class="dv us">Any artifact you can point at — <b>including your own source and private dependencies</b>,
      which no vendor will ever index.</div>

    <div class="dk">Timing</div>
    <div class="dv">After someone else has reported it and the list has shipped.</div>
    <div class="dv us"><b>At scan time.</b> Capabilities are extracted from the artifact itself, so there is no
      list to be added to and no window to sit in.</div>

    <div class="dk">Control</div>
    <div class="dv">Rented per seat or per scan. Your code goes to their servers, and the rule that flagged your
      build isn't yours to read.</div>
    <div class="dv us">Apache-2.0, runs air-gapped, embeddable in what you sell. Every trait, rule and model is
      inspectable — fix a false positive yourself.</div>
  </div>

  {%- set cov = battle | blindSpots(providers) %}
  {%- if cov %}
  <p class="sub" style="margin-top:22px">The first two are measurable, and this run measures them.
    <b>{{ cov.nonPackage }} of {{ cov.cohort }} samples weren't registry packages at all</b> — binaries, executables,
    archives. That is also the shape of your own code.</p>
  <div class="tw">
    <table class="cov">
      <thead>
        <tr><th>Engine</th><th>Couldn't read</th><th>Could look up</th><th>No record yet</th><th>Caught</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        {%- for r in cov.rows %}
        <tr><th scope="row"><i style="background:{{ r.color }}"></i>{{ r.name }}</th>
          <td>{{ r.unreadable }}</td><td class="muted">{{ r.lookups }}</td>
          <td>{{ r.noRecord if r.noRecord else '—' }}</td><td class="muted">{{ r.caught }}</td></tr>
        {%- endfor %}
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
  <p class="fig-note"><b>“No record yet”</b> is the detection gap, measured: a live malicious package the vendor
    indexes and had no entry for at the moment we asked.
    {% for r in cov.clean %}{{ r.name }}{% if not loop.last %}, {% endif %}{% endfor %} read every sample.
    <a class="lnk" href="/scan/how-it-works/">How it decides →</a></p>
  {%- endif %}

  {%- set badSamples = battle.samples | where("label", "bad") -%}
  {%- set cohortBad = badSamples | whereUnset("excluded") -%}
  {%- if curve %}
  <script>
  (function () {
    // Every point is a measurement from this run — atomscan's lvl is swept across the
    // whole grid on each scan, so one pass describes the cohort at every deploy level.
    const C = {{ curve | dump | safe }}, DEF = {{ dialDefault }};
    const el = document.getElementById('dial');
    if (!el || !C.length) return;
    const det = document.querySelector('.proof .n'), fp = document.querySelector('.proof .n.fp');
    const lab = document.getElementById('dial-l'), say = document.getElementById('dial-say');
    const status = document.getElementById('dial-status');
    const stance = (l) => l === DEF ? '— the shipped default, untuned'
      : (l === 0 ? '— zero false-positive budget' : (l < DEF ? '— stricter than the default' : '— tuned for recall'));
    function render() {
      const c = C[+el.value];
      if (det) det.textContent = c.det + '%';
      if (fp) fp.textContent = c.fp + '%';
      lab.textContent = '-l ' + c.l.toLocaleString('en-US');
      say.textContent = stance(c.l);
      el.setAttribute('aria-valuetext', '-l ' + c.l.toLocaleString('en-US') + ': ' + c.det + '% caught, ' + c.flagged + ' false positive' + (c.flagged === 1 ? '' : 's'));
    }
    el.addEventListener('input', render);
    el.addEventListener('change', function () {
      const c = C[+el.value];
      if (status) status.textContent = '-l ' + c.l.toLocaleString('en-US') + ': ' + c.det + '% caught, ' + c.flagged + ' false positive' + (c.flagged === 1 ? '' : 's');
    });
    render();
  })();
  </script>
  {%- endif %}

  <details class="appendix" id="samples">
    <summary>Appendix — samples and methodology <span class="note">all {{ cohortBad | length }}, every one linked</span></summary>
  <div class="samples">
    {%- for sm in cohortBad | sort(false, false, "filename") %}
    <a href="https://lab.atomdrift.org/file/{{ sm.sha256 }}" title="{{ sm.filename }}{% if sm.ecosystem %} · {{ sm.ecosystem }}{% endif %} — view in Atomdrift Lab">{{ sm.purl or sm.filename }}</a>
    {%- endfor %}
  </div>
  <div class="meth"><b>What "0-day" means here.</b> Every detection sample was first seen in the wild within 48
    hours{% if battle.malware_age %} — median {{ battle.malware_age.median_hours | round(0) }} h, youngest
    {{ battle.malware_age.min_hours | round(1) }} h{% endif %}: no signature written for it, no reputation, no
    download history to be anomalous against. Catching malware a feed has already named is a different, easier problem.
    <br><br><b>How this is scored.</b> Every engine gets the identical cohort, and a skip counts as a miss for all of
    them — a file nobody scanned is a file that got through. A listing from a contestant's own feed counts only once an
    independent engine corroborates it. Known-good packages come from the freshest 48 hours of the open-source
    firehose and are re-checked later: one that turns out to be malware leaves that run's false-positive rates, and
    any engine that flagged it is credited with an early detection.
    <b>We run this benchmark and we're one of the engines in it</b>, so every sample, verdict and rate is published.
    {%- if battle.versions %}
    <br><br><b>Engine versions:</b> {% for k, v in battle.versions %}{% if not loop.first %} · {% endif %}{{ providers[k].name or k }} {{ v }}{% endfor %}
    <span style="color:var(--slate)">(locally-run engines; {% for p in providers | bySlot | selectattr("hosted") %}{{ p.name }}{% if not loop.last %}, {% endif %}{% endfor %} are hosted services queried live, so they carry no pinned version).</span>
    {%- endif %}
  </div>
  </details>

  <div class="closer">
    <div>
      <h3>Point it at your own code.</h3>
      <p>Apache-2.0 · runs locally · no account, no index</p>
    </div>
    <div class="inst">curl -fsSL https://install.atomdrift.org/scan.sh | sh</div>
  </div>

</div>
